messages.content:
Build a live metric card control for Uno Platform (Geist and Geist Mono, green on pale green):
- header: "API latency · p95", the latest value with its unit and its change against the start of the window, a Live chip, a 1m / 5m / 15m selector and a pause button;
- a SkiaSharp line chart with a fixed 40–70 axis, an alert line at 65, time labels counting back from now, a live dot with a value tag, one sample a second with the line gliding between samples;
- hover, or focus and use the arrow keys, to inspect a point; Esc closes;
- pause stops at the next sample and shows the time;
- states Connecting (axes reserved), Paused (grey line) and Disconnected (the gap is hatched, Reconnect);
- min, avg, max, window and samples below; a phone layout with the controls at the bottom;
- a page that feeds it from a simulated stream, with a Light/Dark switch, and Hot Design previews of every state.

Stack: Uno Platform single project, SkiaSharp on SKCanvasElement, Material, Toolkit.
